1
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:44,009
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:46,720
[Episode 23]

3
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:50,520
I've seen people steal wallets and phones,

4
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,000
but never a seal.

5
00:01:53,150 --> 00:01:54,070
Sir,

6
00:01:54,350 --> 00:01:55,310
I didn't steal it.

7
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:56,920
It asked me to save it.

8
00:01:58,150 --> 00:01:59,880
So someone else is behind this.

9
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:01,930
Who do you mean?

10
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,000
Yaya.

11
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:04,070
Say no more!

12
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:06,040
Sir,

13
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:07,950
my dad was referring to the seal.

14
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,120
He named the seal Yaya.

15
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,400
Are you two, father and daughter,

16
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,200
on this together and fooling me?

17
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,079
Um,

18
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,280
I-I want to show you something.

19
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:22,430
Could you come out with me for a second?

20
00:02:22,430 --> 00:02:23,280
Please.

21
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:31,050
[This area is under video surveillance.]

22
00:02:26,710 --> 00:02:27,680
Sir,

23
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:28,800
well,

24
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,400
I am

25
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,280
a doctor at Xiaoximen Hospital.

26
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:31,910
My dad

27
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:33,470
has a mental illness.

28
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,190
He is...

29
00:02:34,870 --> 00:02:36,240
not quite right here.

30
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,310
Let me show you his...

31
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:39,680
This is his

32
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,140
psychiatric evaluation.

33
00:02:41,630 --> 00:02:43,360
Why didn't you tell us earlier?

34
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,630
I

35
00:02:46,030 --> 00:02:46,800
was afraid you would

36
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,460
send him to a mental hospital.

37
00:02:51,470 --> 00:02:52,280
I...

38
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,710
My dad has been
on medication continuously.

39
00:02:54,710 --> 00:02:56,520
He has no history of violence.

40
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:58,400
I can take good care of him.

41
00:03:00,030 --> 00:03:00,840
My...

42
00:03:01,710 --> 00:03:03,310
My dad is too kind-hearted.

43
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:04,630
He just

44
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:06,430
wanted to save that seal.

45
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,360
I... I don't know

46
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,470
how he used that tricycle

47
00:03:09,470 --> 00:03:10,910
to haul it out either.

48
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,400
But he really didn't do it for money.

49
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,310
I-I can guarantee t-this.

50
00:03:15,430 --> 00:03:17,360
We don't have the channels either.

51
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:20,540
Your father has a mental illness,

52
00:03:20,590 --> 00:03:21,990
but you are of sound mind.

53
00:03:22,470 --> 00:03:24,280
It's your duty to keep him in check.

54
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,480
Otherwise, if he stole a seal this time,

55
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:27,829
what about next time?

56
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:29,910
What if he steals
something else next time?

57
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:30,710
Exactly.

58
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:31,560
Sir, sorry

59
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:32,710
for all the trouble we've caused you.

60
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:34,640
The point is not the trouble for me.

61
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,360
If your father does this again,

62
00:03:37,630 --> 00:03:39,630
even showing the evaluation won't help.

63
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:41,690
We must send him to a mental hospital.

64
00:03:42,030 --> 00:03:43,280
There won't be a next time.

65
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,140
I promise I will keep him in check.

66
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,360
I don't like

67
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,420
that Officer Song.

68
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:49,079
He's so serious.

69
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:50,590
Given the way he was,

70
00:03:50,590 --> 00:03:51,400
you were still

71
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,030
bowing and scraping to him.

72
00:03:54,030 --> 00:03:55,000
My rank is much higher

73
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,030
than his!

74
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:57,310
I'm wondering

75
00:03:57,310 --> 00:03:59,310
where they put that seal.

76
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,200
I can receive the signal.

77
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:03,100
Let me check the signal

78
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:05,360
to see where they put it.

79
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:07,280
No way.

80
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:09,350
I've got to go find it.

81
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:10,030
It's...

82
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:10,680
Dad!

83
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,790
Can you stop messing around?

84
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:14,030
You pity the seal.

85
00:04:14,030 --> 00:04:15,710
Can you pity me, too?

86
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,040
Me!

87
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,160
Look at me!

88
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,870
Look at me, Dad!

89
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,720
I've been cleaning up

90
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,480
your messes since I was a kid!

91
00:04:24,630 --> 00:04:25,560
Officer Song told me

92
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:26,950
to keep a close eye on you.

93
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:27,750
He said if...

94
00:04:27,750 --> 00:04:28,800
if this happens again,

95
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,730
he'd send you to a mental hospital.

96
00:04:31,390 --> 00:04:32,650
Do you want to go there?

97
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,600
How else can I watch you?

98
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,070
How do you expect me to watch you?

99
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:36,870
Tell me!

100
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:38,870
Every day, all I do is work

101
00:04:38,870 --> 00:04:40,070
and keep an eye on you.

102
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,600
I still want to get my PhD!

103
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:42,920
I want to get out of this place!

104
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,159
But can I?

105
00:04:44,310 --> 00:04:44,800
As if

106
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:45,950
getting out of this place

107
00:04:45,950 --> 00:04:47,950
c-could change my life!

108
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,430
Sober up a bit,

109
00:04:50,430 --> 00:04:51,480
will you?

110
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:56,070
Was I...

111
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,680
Was I born into the wrong family?

112
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:58,630
Why did I have

113
00:04:58,630 --> 00:04:59,800
to get such a fate

114
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,270
and such a dad?

115
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,680
Tell me why...

116
00:05:05,270 --> 00:05:06,190
Why?

117
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:33,310
[Sitong Cold Storage]

118
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:33,240
San,

119
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:33,950
does it have to get

120
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:35,510
your whole family involved?

121
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:36,159
Yes, of course.

122
00:06:36,159 --> 00:06:36,870
Zhengliang,

123
00:06:36,870 --> 00:06:38,560
we are here to cheer for you.

124
00:06:39,270 --> 00:06:40,159
Go for it, brother-in-law!

125
00:06:40,159 --> 00:06:40,870
You got this!

126
00:06:40,870 --> 00:06:41,360
Hey...

127
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:43,360
It's not appropriate
to call me that, is it?

128
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,190
Who are you

129
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:45,920
to decide what others call you?

130
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:51,430
How many of you are going in?

131
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:52,390
The two of us.

132
00:06:52,430 --> 00:06:53,240
Just me.

133
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,040
That won't do.

134
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,750
What if you fall over or get hurt?

135
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:57,950
How can I not worry?

136
00:06:59,630 --> 00:07:00,560
I'll go with you.

137
00:07:00,870 --> 00:07:01,680
Okay.

138
00:07:02,190 --> 00:07:02,830
Any number

139
00:07:02,830 --> 00:07:04,000
of you can go in.

140
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:06,360
As San instructed,

141
00:07:06,390 --> 00:07:08,390
the ground is covered
with 3 layers of ice

142
00:07:08,390 --> 00:07:09,510
and is very slippery. So be careful.

143
00:07:09,510 --> 00:07:10,360
Got it.

144
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:11,930
[Cold Storage Work Notice]

145
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:37,430
Wait a minute!

146
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:40,090
I'll make a call first.

147
00:07:40,159 --> 00:07:41,159
Let me make a call.

148
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:42,190
Okay.

149
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:01,520
What's up?

150
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:02,800
Hello.

151
00:08:03,870 --> 00:08:04,680
Well,

152
00:08:05,510 --> 00:08:07,110
how are you doing in Beijing?

153
00:08:07,430 --> 00:08:08,830
I've been doing great lately.

154
00:08:08,830 --> 00:08:09,960
Beijing is awesome.

155
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,390
My monthly salary is even

156
00:08:11,390 --> 00:08:12,450
higher than yours.

157
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,040
Xiaoximen Hospital is already closed.

158
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,840
Of course you earn more than I do.

159
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:19,390
What made you suddenly

160
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:20,390
call me?

161
00:08:22,510 --> 00:08:23,270
Nothing.

162
00:08:23,630 --> 00:08:24,960
I just called casually.

163
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,400
How have you been lately?

164
00:08:28,430 --> 00:08:29,240
Pretty well?

165
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,360
Just okay.

166
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,669
That's good enough.

167
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:36,580
You are not going
to have a great life anyway.

168
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,120
Zhengguang,

169
00:08:43,150 --> 00:08:44,000
if find it tough

170
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,060
over there, you can always come back.

171
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:48,680
I'm not leaving this winter.

172
00:08:54,030 --> 00:08:55,510
Can I take your word for it?

173
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,130
I've made up my mind.

174
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:02,580
Even if I die,
I want to die in my hometown.

175
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:03,720
Can you

176
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:05,320
please stop jinxing it?

177
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,360
Didn't Mom say

178
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,480
your illness was nothing serious?

179
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,390
Don't think too much.

180
00:09:08,390 --> 00:09:09,270
It won't kill you.

181
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:10,200
Liu Zhengguang!

182
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:19,950
[Problem Parcel Handling Area]

183
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,870
We hired you to work,

184
00:09:13,870 --> 00:09:14,550
not to chit-chat

185
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:15,880
on the phone for so long.

186
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:17,240
Yes,

187
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:19,220
I'll deliver it to you right away.

188
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:20,670
It's an urgent delivery
for a customer, Manager.

189
00:09:19,990 --> 00:09:21,670
[Dumb Liu]

190
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,600
Which customer is called Dumb Liu?

191
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:24,850
[Linmon Express Safety Risk
Grading & Control Checklist]

192
00:09:26,550 --> 00:09:28,550
Don't let him get sick from the cold.

193
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,670
How are you feeling now?

194
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,440
Is it working?

195
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,330
It's freezing cold.

196
00:12:29,670 --> 00:12:30,510
Zhengliang.

197
00:12:32,670 --> 00:12:33,800
Go back to the South.

198
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:36,670
Don't make yourself suffer so much.

199
00:12:39,030 --> 00:12:40,830
I don't want to run away anymore.

200
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,520
What's wrong with running away?

201
00:12:44,870 --> 00:12:45,910
As long as you're healthy

202
00:12:45,910 --> 00:12:47,710
and living well, that's enough.

203
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,240
Why?

204
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:54,390
Why do you always want

205
00:12:54,390 --> 00:12:55,390
to send me away?

206
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:58,080
You did this back then,

207
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,740
and you're still doing it now.

208
00:14:09,990 --> 00:14:12,370
[Fucheng Funeral Services Street]

209
00:14:12,420 --> 00:14:14,630
[Xiao'an Paper Offerings Shop]

210
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:34,120
Girl.

211
00:14:35,790 --> 00:14:36,720
There's a big job

212
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,320
worth 18,000 yuan tomorrow.

213
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:40,600
Order 2,500 yuan's worth of flowers,

214
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:41,720
and work with Xiaozhu tonight

215
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:43,250
to set up the mourning hall.

216
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,840
I don't have time for the next few days.

217
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,510
Liu Zhengliang is having a fever,
with no one else

218
00:14:47,510 --> 00:14:48,240
looking after him.

219
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,480
I've got to take care of him.

220
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:50,600
Just let Xiaozhu

221
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,000
handle it. Won't that do?

222
00:14:53,510 --> 00:14:54,510
It's just a fever.

223
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,320
Will the earth stop turning?

224
00:14:59,630 --> 00:15:00,760
We still need to work

225
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,200
and earn money.

226
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,600
He's been having a fever

227
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:05,510
since his return from the cold storage.

228
00:15:05,510 --> 00:15:06,770
Of course I'm worried.

229
00:15:07,790 --> 00:15:09,360
He's a doctor himself.

230
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:10,970
What are you worried about?

231
00:15:11,790 --> 00:15:13,360
He's good at treating others,

232
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,550
but when it comes to himself,
he's useless.

233
00:15:15,550 --> 00:15:16,600
What a poor thing.

234
00:15:22,750 --> 00:15:23,550
Why don't you

235
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:26,000
call Zhengguang and ask

236
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:27,870
if this has

237
00:15:28,390 --> 00:15:29,750
ever happened before?

238
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:33,510
Okay.

239
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,120
I'll...

240
00:15:35,270 --> 00:15:36,470
I'll call him and see.

241
00:15:40,790 --> 00:15:41,600
Hello?

242
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,460
Delivery for Room 201.

243
00:15:44,550 --> 00:15:46,010
Leave it at the door? Okay.

244
00:15:46,550 --> 00:15:47,240
No problem.

245
00:15:57,030 --> 00:15:58,240
Chen, what's up?

246
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:02,120
He's sick?

247
00:16:03,870 --> 00:16:04,600
I don't know.

248
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:05,330
I don't think

249
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:06,720
it has happened before.

250
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:07,910
He didn't come back often.

251
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:10,040
I don't recall this happening before.

252
00:16:11,750 --> 00:16:12,550
Okay.

253
00:16:14,150 --> 00:16:14,750
Alright.

254
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:19,440
Come in.

255
00:16:21,630 --> 00:16:22,440
Manager.

256
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:25,150
What is it?

257
00:16:27,150 --> 00:16:28,680
I'd like to ask for 3 days off

258
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,430
to go back to my hometown.

259
00:16:34,670 --> 00:16:35,870
What for?

260
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,270
My brother is sick.

261
00:16:37,670 --> 00:16:39,600
I want to go back and check in on him.

262
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:41,280
What illness?

263
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:45,870
It's quite complicated.

264
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:46,670
I can't really

265
00:16:46,670 --> 00:16:47,480
explain it clearly right now,

266
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:48,870
but it's quite serious.

267
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:50,960
Okay, you may go back.

268
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:52,970
Thank you, Manager.

269
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,600
We will pay you

270
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:56,640
for this month before you leave,

271
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:58,790
and you don't need to come back.

272
00:17:03,270 --> 00:17:03,910
What do you mean, Manager?

273
00:17:03,910 --> 00:17:05,040
I don't quite get it.

274
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:07,240
Am I not making myself

275
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:08,680
clear enough?

276
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:12,240
Manager Wu wasn't

277
00:17:12,310 --> 00:17:13,240
making it hard for you specifically.

278
00:17:13,210 --> 00:17:20,540
[Dumplings]

279
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,790
He treats every one of us the same way.

280
00:17:15,790 --> 00:17:17,160
I've been working here for 3 years.

281
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,510
I've only taken 1 day off.

282
00:17:18,510 --> 00:17:20,270
You've only been here for a few months,

283
00:17:20,270 --> 00:17:21,930
and you want to take 3 days off.

284
00:17:22,030 --> 00:17:23,030
No way.

285
00:17:25,270 --> 00:17:26,240
But mine should be

286
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,440
considered an exemption.

287
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,500
My brother is sick.

288
00:17:28,510 --> 00:17:30,310
What's the use of you going back?

289
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:32,110
You might as well make more money

290
00:17:32,110 --> 00:17:33,710
to transfer to your brother.

291
00:17:35,550 --> 00:17:37,110
I don't even have enough for myself.

292
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:38,310
How can I transfer it?

293
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:42,740
I don't know what else I can say to you.

294
00:17:46,350 --> 00:17:47,510
Just think about it.

295
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:49,140
I'm going to the restroom.

296
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:03,300
[Dumb Liu]

297
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,590
Why haven't you been pushing me

298
00:18:38,590 --> 00:18:40,450
to snap the rubber band recently?

299
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:43,270
I gave up!

300
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:46,240
You gave up so easily?

301
00:18:46,750 --> 00:18:48,400
Why don't you learn from those two?

302
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:49,460
I can't learn that.

303
00:18:50,590 --> 00:18:52,030
The two of them treat each other

304
00:18:52,030 --> 00:18:53,240
as equals.

305
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:55,640
And you are...

306
00:18:56,590 --> 00:18:57,400
my leader.

307
00:18:58,070 --> 00:19:00,000
I dare not speak up.

308
00:19:02,310 --> 00:19:03,310
Where's the disc?

309
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:06,270
I didn't see it in the machine.

310
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:14,660
You've figured it out?

311
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,030
What do you mean?

312
00:19:18,030 --> 00:19:18,960
To get treated.

313
00:19:19,030 --> 00:19:19,880
I'm not sick.

314
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:25,680
Then why are you looking for the disc?

315
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:27,240
Can't I just give it a try?

316
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,100
You want to destroy it, right?

317
00:19:30,030 --> 00:19:32,160
I'm doing it for our daughter, Ai Chen.

318
00:19:34,070 --> 00:19:35,070
This is all very normal.

319
00:19:35,070 --> 00:19:36,530
You need to exercise more.

320
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:38,640
Yeah, yeah, you have to keep it up.

321
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:39,270
Exercise a bit,

322
00:19:39,270 --> 00:19:40,550
but don't overdo it.

323
00:19:40,790 --> 00:19:42,110
Adjust your diet, too.

324
00:19:42,350 --> 00:19:43,070
Like oil.

325
00:19:43,070 --> 00:19:44,480
Too much oil and salt is not good.

326
00:19:44,030 --> 00:19:47,590
[Medical Consultation] [Free]

327
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:45,680
Okay, bye.

328
00:19:47,750 --> 00:19:49,160
[Former President of Xiaoximen Hospital]

329
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,350
The diastolic pressure is over 90. Good.

330
00:19:49,350 --> 00:19:50,510
Do you exercise usually?

331
00:19:50,510 --> 00:19:51,350
Keep it up.

332
00:19:51,590 --> 00:19:53,320
And pay attention to your diet.

333
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:56,590
I had been working
as an administrator for so long.

334
00:19:56,590 --> 00:19:58,480
I've almost forgotten I'm a doctor.

335
00:19:58,480 --> 00:19:59,510
You've never been

336
00:19:59,590 --> 00:20:00,880
a doctor in my heart.

337
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:04,420
You were born to be a hospital president.

338
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:05,830
You have that kind

339
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:06,960
of leadership charisma.

340
00:20:06,670 --> 00:20:08,690
[Former President of Xiaoximen Hospital]

341
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:08,830
I feel very sad

342
00:20:08,830 --> 00:20:10,110
hearing you say that.

343
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:11,290
[Former President of Xiaoximen Hospital]

344
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:11,720
What's there to be sad about?

345
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,110
You don't even want to be a leader,

346
00:20:13,110 --> 00:20:13,640
do you?

347
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:15,580
Doctor, I feel a little dizzy.

348
00:20:15,590 --> 00:20:16,850
You are the President?

349
00:20:17,110 --> 00:20:18,170
Former President.

350
00:20:18,750 --> 00:20:19,720
What do you mean?

351
00:20:20,110 --> 00:20:21,640
Aren't you President Long?

352
00:20:24,790 --> 00:20:25,680
I used to be the President,

353
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:26,720
but not anymore.

354
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:29,160
Then do your words carry weight now?

355
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:31,270
Well, that depends.

356
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:33,070
I want you

357
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:34,550
to arrange a job for my son.

358
00:20:34,790 --> 00:20:35,640
Can you do it?

359
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,000
What kind of job does your son want?

360
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:40,880
We don't have high expectations.

361
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:42,350
A permanent position is fine.

362
00:20:42,350 --> 00:20:44,610
The workplace is preferably in the city.

363
00:20:45,830 --> 00:20:46,750
If I could find

364
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:47,720
a job like that,

365
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:49,690
I wouldn't be sitting here.

366
00:20:50,110 --> 00:20:51,000
No way.

367
00:20:51,550 --> 00:20:52,270
Then you're just

368
00:20:52,270 --> 00:20:53,550
an average president.

369
00:20:55,270 --> 00:20:56,880
Just... Just use this prescription

370
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:58,830
[Former President of Xiaoximen Hospital]

371
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,250
to improve your health.

372
00:20:58,270 --> 00:20:59,000
Okay.

373
00:21:01,350 --> 00:21:02,160
Mr. Long.

374
00:21:03,590 --> 00:21:04,480
Huang.

375
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:07,030
I heard you guys are
doing a free clinic here.

376
00:21:07,030 --> 00:21:08,590
I bought some walnut cookies
on my way here,

377
00:21:08,590 --> 00:21:10,720
so you can grab a bite if you're hungry.

378
00:21:12,550 --> 00:21:13,240
Nice.

379
00:21:13,550 --> 00:21:15,810
There happens to be no one here right now.

380
00:21:15,830 --> 00:21:16,790
Are you available?

381
00:21:16,790 --> 00:21:17,680
I have no patients here.

382
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,210
But the two of them are busy.

383
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,920
Can you take some time
to check on Liu Zhengliang?

384
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:22,720
What's wrong?

385
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:23,680
He's sick.

386
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:26,140
I'm afraid
he might take a turn for the worse.

387
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:28,160
[Former President of Xiaoximen Hospital]

388
00:21:32,270 --> 00:21:33,200
Liu Zhengliang.

389
00:21:33,790 --> 00:21:34,720
Liu Zhengliang.

390
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:35,720
Liu Zhengliang.

391
00:21:42,070 --> 00:21:43,330
What's wrong with you?

392
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:45,720
Pay up.

393
00:21:45,830 --> 00:21:46,760
You lost the bet.

394
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:48,550
You're awake?

395
00:21:49,750 --> 00:21:51,010
Have some fruit, guys.

396
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:52,550
I admit defeat.

397
00:21:54,590 --> 00:21:55,650
What are you doing?

398
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:57,810
-They just made a bet
-Impressive.

399
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,030
and guessed what your first words

400
00:21:59,030 --> 00:22:00,200
would be after waking up.

401
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:01,640
President Long... won?

402
00:22:01,790 --> 00:22:02,720
Then you must have said,

403
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:04,120
"What's wrong with you?"

404
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,160
I originally guessed

405
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:06,030
that your first words

406
00:22:06,030 --> 00:22:07,640
would definitely be swearing.

407
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:09,270
That was way off.

408
00:22:09,270 --> 00:22:10,830
He's a gentleman.

409
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:11,960
How could he possibly swear?

410
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:12,960
I guessed that

411
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,760
you would jump up with a big yelp.

412
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:23,440
I think there's really something wrong
with you guys.

413
00:22:24,510 --> 00:22:25,710
I didn't want to come.

414
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:28,690
Ai Chen said you had a high fever

415
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:30,590
and forced us to come and check on you.

416
00:22:30,590 --> 00:22:32,520
Let me see if you're having a fever.

417
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:35,480
There seems to be a slight fever.

418
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:37,590
Are you done checking?

419
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:38,440
Leave now if you are done.

420
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:39,680
I still need to rest.

421
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,200
No rush.

422
00:22:41,790 --> 00:22:43,070
You're not cured yet.

423
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:46,110
Even I couldn't cure myself.

424
00:22:46,110 --> 00:22:47,310
Can you cure me?

425
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:48,960
Emotional wounds

426
00:22:49,110 --> 00:22:51,640
need emotional healing.

427
00:22:53,270 --> 00:22:54,440
Even if they can't cure him,

428
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:56,070
at least they can give him

429
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:57,160
some peace of mind.

430
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:58,510
Yes, exactly.

431
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:03,440
Xiaoximen Hospital

432
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:05,720
won't be closed forever.

433
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:07,240
Don't ask me

434
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:07,750
any questions.

435
00:23:07,750 --> 00:23:09,680
Don't ask me what method I will use.

436
00:23:10,750 --> 00:23:11,550
I can only assure you

437
00:23:11,550 --> 00:23:13,080
that I'll have it open soon.

438
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:18,400
You can also continue to work at Xiaoximen

439
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,600
for many, many years.

440
00:23:24,270 --> 00:23:25,680
How is this good news?

441
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:36,550
I think I

442
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:37,880
promised him before.

443
00:23:38,790 --> 00:23:39,440
I promised

444
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:41,570
to give him a room with sealed windows.

445
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:44,370
Now I've decided to add something.

446
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,920
He can take days off when it snows,

447
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:48,920
with full pay,

448
00:23:49,350 --> 00:23:50,810
and keep the special room.

449
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:53,110
And when it snows,

450
00:23:53,110 --> 00:23:53,880
I'll immediately

451
00:23:53,880 --> 00:23:55,350
have someone shovel all the snow away.

452
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:56,070
Of course,

453
00:23:56,350 --> 00:23:57,880
only inside the hospital.

454
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:02,880
This is the best

455
00:24:05,070 --> 00:24:06,110
I can do.

456
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:19,510
That's all?

457
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:20,480
What?

458
00:24:21,310 --> 00:24:22,640
Is this not good enough?

459
00:24:25,110 --> 00:24:25,920
There's more.

460
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:33,900
I won't force you to get treated anymore.

461
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:37,880
I mean what I say.

462
00:24:47,030 --> 00:24:48,030
I want to treat it.

463
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:49,640
Help me get access
to the cold storage again.

464
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:51,100
I want to try one more time.

465
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:56,310
He's hopeless.

466
00:24:58,720 --> 00:24:59,510
Hopeless.

467
00:25:01,110 --> 00:25:01,960
Hopeless.

468
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,240
Serves you right.

469
00:25:15,960 --> 00:25:17,030
Interesting.

470
00:25:17,030 --> 00:25:17,960
Come here, too.

471
00:25:18,680 --> 00:25:22,030
You now look more like a local than I do.

472
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:28,100
If there's really no other way,
I'll just stay here.

473
00:25:29,750 --> 00:25:31,880
What are you laughing at?
What do you mean?

474
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:33,110
It's fine by me.

475
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:34,810
But the point is,

476
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:36,830
can you let go of Fucheng?

477
00:25:37,110 --> 00:25:38,880
What have I got to lose?

478
00:25:39,480 --> 00:25:41,680
I have nothing there but my parents.

479
00:25:44,110 --> 00:25:45,270
I don't

480
00:25:46,510 --> 00:25:47,440
think so.

481
00:25:51,400 --> 00:25:52,330
What do you mean?

482
00:25:54,640 --> 00:25:56,160
Last time I went back,

483
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:58,440
we were eating at Mingming's house,

484
00:25:58,440 --> 00:26:00,040
and you showed up uninvited.

485
00:26:00,310 --> 00:26:01,000
You kept

486
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,440
glancing at her.

487
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:04,880
What was that?

488
00:26:05,960 --> 00:26:07,220
Do you think I'm a fool?

489
00:26:08,550 --> 00:26:09,550
Do you think I couldn't tell

490
00:26:09,550 --> 00:26:10,810
your feelings for her?

491
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:17,750
Yes.

492
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:20,900
I do have feelings for her.

493
00:26:22,720 --> 00:26:24,110
She's the kind of girl

494
00:26:25,070 --> 00:26:26,160
who works hard

495
00:26:26,640 --> 00:26:27,840
and tries to get a PhD.

496
00:26:29,880 --> 00:26:30,550
Given the way I am,

497
00:26:30,550 --> 00:26:32,610
if I were her, I'd look down on me, too.

498
00:26:34,920 --> 00:26:36,160
Come on, man,

499
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:39,240
you sound just like I used to.

500
00:26:39,790 --> 00:26:40,960
I was also like that.

501
00:26:41,640 --> 00:26:42,640
I hated it when she told me

502
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:43,680
what to do,

503
00:26:44,310 --> 00:26:45,640
urged me to study,

504
00:26:45,830 --> 00:26:47,830
and always tried to keep me in check.

505
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:51,240
Wasn't that all for your own good?

506
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:52,550
She wants a chance to study,

507
00:26:52,550 --> 00:26:54,080
but she can't even have one.

508
00:26:55,030 --> 00:26:56,070
She just hoped

509
00:26:57,590 --> 00:26:58,990
for the people around her

510
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:01,530
to leave no regrets, right?

511
00:27:09,550 --> 00:27:10,790
I still

512
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:13,350
owe her an apology.

513
00:27:15,680 --> 00:27:16,480
Chen Junnan.

514
00:27:21,110 --> 00:27:23,110
I think you know her better than I do.

515
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:52,240
Mingming,

516
00:27:52,720 --> 00:27:54,110
has something gone wrong

517
00:27:54,110 --> 00:27:55,710
at your workplace recently?

518
00:27:57,070 --> 00:27:57,830
Nope.

519
00:27:57,830 --> 00:27:58,550
W-What's wrong?

520
00:27:58,550 --> 00:27:59,350
What's wrong?

521
00:28:00,070 --> 00:28:00,880
Why hasn't

522
00:28:00,880 --> 00:28:02,640
Commissioner Chen come lately?

523
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:03,480
Who?

524
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:05,130
Commissioner Chen,

525
00:28:05,240 --> 00:28:06,590
the one who came to our place for dinner

526
00:28:06,590 --> 00:28:08,190
and brought pizza last time.

527
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:11,800
Commissioner Chen is a brilliant comrade.

528
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:13,350
This comrade

529
00:28:14,070 --> 00:28:16,400
has been undercover
in the hospital for a long time,

530
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:17,270
making

531
00:28:17,310 --> 00:28:19,710
great contributions to the organization.

532
00:28:19,750 --> 00:28:21,280
But what is he busy with now?

533
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:25,590
Mingming,

534
00:28:25,590 --> 00:28:26,720
what is he busy with?

535
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:28,240
Mingming?

536
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:30,640
How do I know

537
00:28:30,640 --> 00:28:31,880
what he's busy with?

538
00:28:32,070 --> 00:28:33,640
You are colleagues in the same workplace!

539
00:28:33,640 --> 00:28:34,440
How could you not know

540
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:35,640
what he's been doing?

541
00:28:39,590 --> 00:28:40,680
I got it.

542
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:44,000
I probably have been abandoned

543
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,480
by the organization.

544
00:28:45,830 --> 00:28:47,750
I feel very uneasy.

545
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:50,350
You'd better ask him

546
00:28:50,350 --> 00:28:51,310
what's going on.

547
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:02,750
It works!

548
00:29:03,480 --> 00:29:06,210
The signal's much better today
than two days ago.

549
00:29:10,430 --> 00:29:11,760
[Xiaoximen is closed down.]

550
00:29:11,780 --> 00:29:13,300
[Are you not going to come back?]

551
00:29:24,030 --> 00:29:24,830
Hello?

552
00:29:27,030 --> 00:29:27,790
It's me.

553
00:29:30,270 --> 00:29:31,930
It's really hard to reach you.

554
00:29:32,110 --> 00:29:34,310
I thought you were taken away by aliens.

555
00:29:36,270 --> 00:29:37,400
Well, um,

556
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:40,640
the signal here is intermittent.

557
00:29:43,550 --> 00:29:44,790
H-How are you doing?

558
00:29:47,310 --> 00:29:48,570
I'm doing pretty fine.

559
00:30:02,350 --> 00:30:03,680
Is there anything else?

560
00:30:08,240 --> 00:30:09,070
Well,

561
00:30:09,350 --> 00:30:10,270
Zhengliang's been

562
00:30:10,270 --> 00:30:11,800
having a rough time lately.

563
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:15,790
What's wrong?

564
00:30:16,510 --> 00:30:18,720
He's treating his chionophobia.

565
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:20,400
He's been having a fever.

566
00:30:24,680 --> 00:30:25,590
I see.

567
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:30,510
That's all. I'll hang up.

568
00:30:31,070 --> 00:30:31,880
Bye.

569
00:30:45,880 --> 00:30:47,790
You've been here for so long.

570
00:30:47,960 --> 00:30:49,640
I only taught you how to work

571
00:30:49,790 --> 00:30:51,590
but didn't teach you any skills.

572
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:54,480
You were teaching me skills

573
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:56,410
when you told me how to work, right?

574
00:30:57,270 --> 00:30:59,270
Our ethnic minorities
in the Greater Khingan Mountains

575
00:30:59,270 --> 00:31:00,240
have a song we often sing.

576
00:31:00,240 --> 00:31:01,270
I'll teach you.

577
00:31:01,750 --> 00:31:02,550
Okay.

578
00:31:02,790 --> 00:31:03,790
When you leave in the future,

579
00:31:03,790 --> 00:31:04,990
you can brag about it.

580
00:31:05,270 --> 00:31:06,880
It's not a wasted trip, right?

581
00:31:06,880 --> 00:31:08,740
I'll sing it to them when I go back.

582
00:31:09,790 --> 00:31:11,030
Sing after me.

583
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:14,830
There's a vast forest

584
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:17,110
in the Greater Khingan Mountains.

585
00:31:19,270 --> 00:31:21,790
There's a vast forest

586
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:24,070
in the Greater Khingan Mountains.

587
00:31:24,510 --> 00:31:26,960
In the forest live

588
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:29,160
the brave Oroqen people.

589
00:31:29,590 --> 00:31:32,000
In the forest live

590
00:31:32,110 --> 00:31:34,160
the brave Oroqen people.

591
00:31:34,550 --> 00:31:37,030
A sturdy steed

592
00:31:37,070 --> 00:31:38,880
and a gun.

593
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:41,790
A sturdy steed

594
00:31:41,960 --> 00:31:43,960
and a gun.

595
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:46,590
There's a vast forest

596
00:31:46,590 --> 00:31:48,270
in the Greater Khingan Mountains.

597
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:51,030
In the forest live

598
00:31:51,070 --> 00:31:52,790
the brave Oroqen people.

599
00:31:53,240 --> 00:31:55,310
A sturdy steed

600
00:31:55,350 --> 00:31:57,160
and a gun.

601
00:31:57,480 --> 00:31:59,590
The mountains abound
with all kinds of deer,

602
00:31:59,590 --> 00:32:01,240
more than you could ever count.

603
00:32:09,480 --> 00:32:11,240
You don't have to take
such good care of me.

604
00:32:11,240 --> 00:32:13,100
It's not like I'm terminally ill.

605
00:32:14,480 --> 00:32:16,480
You're really feeling better, huh?

606
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:18,240
Listen.

607
00:32:19,550 --> 00:32:20,920
I'll do whatever I want.

608
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:21,830
Leave me alone.

609
00:32:24,110 --> 00:32:25,790
Stop wasting your time on me.

610
00:32:25,960 --> 00:32:27,760
Pay more attention to yourself.

611
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:30,880
What do you mean by that?

612
00:32:33,350 --> 00:32:35,280
Do something that makes you happy.

613
00:32:36,590 --> 00:32:37,720
Then I did it right.

614
00:32:37,720 --> 00:32:39,180
I'm super happy right now.

615
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:43,880
At least

616
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:45,240
don't delay your work.

617
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:47,590
I heard you declined several orders.

618
00:32:47,590 --> 00:32:48,350
Is that true?

619
00:32:49,880 --> 00:32:51,740
Can you stop listening to rumors?

620
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:53,590
When did I ever delay my work?

621
00:32:53,590 --> 00:32:54,070
I...

622
00:32:54,400 --> 00:32:56,660
I do my work
all in the middle of the night.

623
00:32:56,790 --> 00:32:58,440
It's just a few less hours of sleep.

624
00:32:58,440 --> 00:32:59,200
No big deal.

625
00:33:03,790 --> 00:33:04,590
You know what?

626
00:33:05,350 --> 00:33:06,400
Just because you've

627
00:33:06,400 --> 00:33:08,030
got a few more years of schooling

628
00:33:08,030 --> 00:33:09,720
doesn't mean you can lecture me.

629
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:11,320
Do you think I'm an imbecile?

630
00:33:12,310 --> 00:33:13,570
People are different.

631
00:33:14,400 --> 00:33:15,110
Not everyone

632
00:33:15,110 --> 00:33:16,750
puts money first,

633
00:33:16,750 --> 00:33:17,510
you know?

634
00:33:18,350 --> 00:33:19,160
What?

635
00:33:19,510 --> 00:33:20,910
Is going out to work hard,

636
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:22,790
having whatever

637
00:33:22,790 --> 00:33:23,920
you want,

638
00:33:23,920 --> 00:33:25,200
and wearing pretty clothes

639
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:27,060
the only way to satisfy yourself?

640
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:28,440
Nope.

641
00:33:29,350 --> 00:33:30,510
Treating you well

642
00:33:31,310 --> 00:33:32,470
just makes me happy,

643
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:33,940
and that's enough.

644
00:33:35,070 --> 00:33:36,270
What else do you want?

645
00:33:38,830 --> 00:33:40,200
What else can I ask for?

646
00:33:41,350 --> 00:33:42,310
You don't know?

647
00:33:42,310 --> 00:33:43,680
Let me tell you.

648
00:33:45,270 --> 00:33:47,070
When you get along with someone,

649
00:33:47,510 --> 00:33:48,310
treating them well

650
00:33:48,310 --> 00:33:49,790
is not about causing them

651
00:33:49,790 --> 00:33:51,000
less trouble.

652
00:33:51,270 --> 00:33:52,070
No.

653
00:33:52,750 --> 00:33:54,790
It's about being sincere.

654
00:33:56,270 --> 00:33:57,110
It means that

655
00:33:57,640 --> 00:33:59,000
you should share

656
00:33:59,880 --> 00:34:01,110
good news with me

657
00:34:01,590 --> 00:34:03,030
and ask for help

658
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:04,770
when you're in trouble.

659
00:34:04,790 --> 00:34:06,510
Right? That's treating others well.

660
00:34:06,510 --> 00:34:07,830
Instead of worrying over nothing,

661
00:34:07,830 --> 00:34:08,489
it's better

662
00:34:09,150 --> 00:34:11,030
to have some barbecue together.

663
00:34:12,030 --> 00:34:13,030
Isn't that great?

664
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:17,760
I don't understand

665
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:18,710
your gibberish.

666
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:21,130
I'm almost done eating.

667
00:34:21,510 --> 00:34:22,710
I'm going to lie down.

668
00:34:23,800 --> 00:34:25,530
You're going to lie down again?

669
00:34:26,030 --> 00:34:26,800
Stop,

670
00:34:26,840 --> 00:34:28,230
let's go for a walk.

671
00:34:29,190 --> 00:34:30,800
Let's get some fresh air.

672
00:34:32,280 --> 00:34:33,880
There's nowhere I want to go.

673
00:34:34,360 --> 00:34:36,400
Let's go to the train station, shall we?

674
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:37,929
Why go to the train station?

675
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:40,440
Go with me to pick up a friend.

676
00:34:41,949 --> 00:34:45,340
[Welcome to Fucheng Station]

677
00:34:47,550 --> 00:34:48,510
Still cold, right?

678
00:34:48,510 --> 00:34:49,360
Come this way.

679
00:34:49,480 --> 00:34:50,080
It's fine.

680
00:34:50,550 --> 00:34:51,550
Here, put this on.

681
00:34:52,710 --> 00:34:53,710
What are you doing?

682
00:34:53,710 --> 00:34:54,440
No need.

683
00:34:54,440 --> 00:34:55,230
Shut up.

684
00:34:56,880 --> 00:34:58,140
How dare you pull away?

685
00:35:03,110 --> 00:35:04,310
You look really good.

686
00:35:09,670 --> 00:35:10,710
You look good!

687
00:35:10,710 --> 00:35:11,510
How annoying.

688
00:35:12,280 --> 00:35:14,230
You look really good now.

689
00:35:14,230 --> 00:35:15,000
Handsome!

690
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:16,110
Absolutely!

691
00:35:16,230 --> 00:35:17,150
What did you do?

692
00:35:17,150 --> 00:35:18,000
Look...

693
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:19,150
Why is your face all chapped?

694
00:35:19,150 --> 00:35:20,070
What happened?

695
00:35:20,110 --> 00:35:21,070
I've gone to play with deer

696
00:35:21,070 --> 00:35:22,440
in the Greater Khingan Mountains, right?

697
00:35:22,440 --> 00:35:23,230
Reindeer!

698
00:35:23,280 --> 00:35:24,440
It had worms in its stomach.

699
00:35:24,440 --> 00:35:25,440
I smoked it,

700
00:35:25,440 --> 00:35:26,480
and it turned me into this.

701
00:35:26,480 --> 00:35:28,320
Did you smoke the deer or yourself?

702
00:35:28,320 --> 00:35:30,150
There's a vast forest

703
00:35:30,150 --> 00:35:31,760
in the Greater Khingan Mountains.

704
00:35:31,880 --> 00:35:33,920
In the forest live

705
00:35:33,920 --> 00:35:35,630
the brave Oroqen people.

706
00:35:36,030 --> 00:35:38,030
A sturdy steed

707
00:35:38,150 --> 00:35:39,560
and a gun.

708
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,880
The mountains abound
with all kinds of deer,

709
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:43,320
too many to eliminate.

710
00:35:43,760 --> 00:35:44,710
Everyone's looking at you.

711
00:35:44,710 --> 00:35:45,440
Enough.

712
00:35:45,960 --> 00:35:47,220
It's good you're back.

713
00:35:48,550 --> 00:35:50,080
It's good you didn't leave.

714
00:35:51,960 --> 00:35:53,690
I'll teach you throat singing.

715
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:02,590
I heard from Mingming

716
00:36:01,850 --> 00:36:06,460
[Vacant]

717
00:36:02,590 --> 00:36:04,550
that you've had a persistent fever lately.

718
00:36:04,550 --> 00:36:05,480
What's going on?

719
00:36:06,760 --> 00:36:08,690
It's alright. I've recovered now.

720
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:09,620
Say that again.

721
00:36:10,710 --> 00:36:11,590
I took your temperature

722
00:36:11,590 --> 00:36:13,800
this morning,
and it was still 37.8 degrees.

723
00:36:13,800 --> 00:36:15,360
This constant low fever is no good.

724
00:36:15,360 --> 00:36:16,710
Is it a virus, or an infection,

725
00:36:16,710 --> 00:36:17,480
or what?

726
00:36:17,480 --> 00:36:18,760
Don't burn your lungs out.

727
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:20,150
Alright, enough about me.

728
00:36:20,150 --> 00:36:21,350
Let's talk about you.

729
00:36:21,590 --> 00:36:22,720
What are your plans?

730
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:24,960
Are you going back to No. 1 Hospital?

731
00:36:26,280 --> 00:36:27,320
Now that I'm back after being away

732
00:36:27,320 --> 00:36:28,510
for days, I definitely have to handle

733
00:36:28,510 --> 00:36:29,910
the urgent things first.

734
00:36:30,710 --> 00:36:32,510
There is something urgent here.

735
00:36:32,750 --> 00:36:34,190
Persuade your buddy

736
00:36:34,320 --> 00:36:35,580
not to push his limits.

737
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:37,740
What? What do you mean?

738
00:36:39,440 --> 00:36:41,440
Do you know about exposure therapy?

739
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:44,230
It's about locking him in a cold storage

740
00:36:44,760 --> 00:36:46,760
and forcing him to face ice and snow.

741
00:36:48,480 --> 00:36:50,080
Isn't that suicide therapy?

742
00:36:50,590 --> 00:36:52,520
Is it the reason why you got a fever?

743
00:36:55,710 --> 00:36:56,710
Whose idea was it?

744
00:36:58,840 --> 00:36:59,630
Mine.

745
00:37:00,150 --> 00:37:01,480
But I've changed my mind now.

746
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:02,590
I can't bear

747
00:37:02,590 --> 00:37:03,920
to see him in this state.

748
00:37:04,630 --> 00:37:05,960
You can't bear to see it?

749
00:37:06,230 --> 00:37:07,560
What did you say before?

750
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:08,840
That was before.

751
00:37:08,960 --> 00:37:10,440
I've changed my mind now.

752
00:37:11,070 --> 00:37:12,190
Women are fickle,

753
00:37:12,190 --> 00:37:13,030
you know?

754
00:37:14,030 --> 00:37:16,030
Let's not force anything, okay?

755
00:37:18,070 --> 00:37:19,530
Wait, let me sort this out.

756
00:37:20,110 --> 00:37:21,440
So basically,

757
00:37:22,190 --> 00:37:24,590
he wants to continue to stimulate himself.

758
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:27,330
Ai Chen feels bad for you

759
00:37:27,550 --> 00:37:29,440
and doesn't want you to continue,

760
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:30,150
right?

761
00:37:31,880 --> 00:37:32,710
That's pretty much it.

762
00:37:32,710 --> 00:37:34,320
What do you mean, pretty much?

763
00:37:34,320 --> 00:37:36,000
When did I feel bad for you?

764
00:37:37,070 --> 00:37:38,670
A-Am I that sentimental?

765
00:37:39,480 --> 00:37:40,800
I'm afraid this might wear him out.

766
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,230
What if his illness gets worse?

767
00:37:42,230 --> 00:37:43,290
Yes, I understand.

768
00:37:43,400 --> 00:37:45,280
But I still support Dr. Liu.

769
00:37:45,920 --> 00:37:47,180
If it doesn't kill him,

770
00:37:48,110 --> 00:37:49,840
just treat him to death, right?

771
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:52,400
But come to think of it,

772
00:37:52,630 --> 00:37:53,440
if I die,

773
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:54,500
what should you do?

774
00:37:55,550 --> 00:37:56,800
That's quite convenient.

775
00:37:56,800 --> 00:37:57,920
Her whole family can send you off.

776
00:37:57,920 --> 00:37:59,050
A one-stop service.

777
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:00,860
Say that again!

778
00:38:00,960 --> 00:38:02,000
You're so annoying, aren't you?

779
00:38:02,000 --> 00:38:03,460
But that's true, isn't it?

780
00:38:05,320 --> 00:38:06,710
But listen,

781
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:09,400
I'm serious this time.

782
00:38:21,710 --> 00:38:23,030
Ai, you're back?

783
00:38:32,510 --> 00:38:33,320
Ai Chen.

784
00:38:34,960 --> 00:38:35,760
Ai Chen...

785
00:38:52,840 --> 00:38:54,370
Isn't this Ai Chen's scarf?

786
00:38:54,760 --> 00:38:56,440
Why is it around your neck?

787
00:38:58,500 --> 00:39:02,740
[Gas Safety Reminder:
Gas safety concerns every household.]

788
00:38:59,070 --> 00:39:00,280
She lent it to me.

789
00:39:00,710 --> 00:39:01,440
You can just

790
00:39:01,440 --> 00:39:02,110
take it back to her.

791
00:39:02,110 --> 00:39:02,880
No need.

792
00:39:02,920 --> 00:39:03,710
Keep it on.

793
00:39:05,030 --> 00:39:06,160
It looks good on you.

794
00:39:08,440 --> 00:39:09,590
Let's talk inside,

795
00:39:09,590 --> 00:39:10,150
Mrs. Mi Si.

796
00:39:10,150 --> 00:39:10,840
Come on.

797
00:39:20,150 --> 00:39:22,010
I'm more familiar with this house

798
00:39:22,150 --> 00:39:23,190
than you are.

799
00:39:24,960 --> 00:39:27,020
I used to come here often when your mom

800
00:39:27,320 --> 00:39:28,190
was alive.

801
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:32,840
Whenever she got sick,

802
00:39:34,190 --> 00:39:35,920
I was the one taking care of her.

803
00:39:39,030 --> 00:39:40,000
I don't seem

804
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:41,030
to have any memory

805
00:39:41,030 --> 00:39:42,440
of seeing my mom sick.

806
00:39:45,070 --> 00:39:46,670
Maybe I saw it when I was a kid,

807
00:39:47,030 --> 00:39:48,190
but it's been so long

808
00:39:48,190 --> 00:39:49,450
that I don't remember.

809
00:39:50,630 --> 00:39:51,590
So I always thought

810
00:39:51,590 --> 00:39:53,070
my mom was in good health.

811
00:39:55,760 --> 00:39:57,560
Being a doctor for so many years,

812
00:39:58,800 --> 00:39:59,670
I never asked her

813
00:39:59,670 --> 00:40:00,670
about her health.

814
00:40:02,670 --> 00:40:03,600
Do you regret it?

815
00:40:09,230 --> 00:40:10,030
Your mom

816
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:13,400
always shared the good news,
never the bad.

817
00:40:14,280 --> 00:40:16,080
She kept her troubles to herself

818
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:18,330
and never wanted to bother others.

819
00:40:19,510 --> 00:40:20,510
But she was

820
00:40:20,840 --> 00:40:21,590
very sensitive,

821
00:40:21,590 --> 00:40:24,070
fragile, and kind.

822
00:40:27,070 --> 00:40:28,330
Are you also like that?

823
00:40:33,150 --> 00:40:34,030
I don't know.

824
00:40:36,670 --> 00:40:37,550
Do you know that your mom

825
00:40:37,550 --> 00:40:39,550
visited your dad's grave every year

826
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:41,300
and stayed at the cemetery

827
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:43,110
for a whole day each time?

828
00:40:45,360 --> 00:40:46,150
No, I don't.

829
00:40:48,030 --> 00:40:48,760
Then do you know

830
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:50,440
why I came to see you today?

831
00:41:02,400 --> 00:41:03,190
Look.

832
00:41:04,110 --> 00:41:05,800
I used your treatment method

833
00:41:06,110 --> 00:41:08,770
and snapped myself
with a rubber band all night.

834
00:41:14,550 --> 00:41:15,550
For the first time

835
00:41:16,630 --> 00:41:18,830
in so many years, I've admitted I'm sick

836
00:41:19,550 --> 00:41:21,590
and been willing to get treated.

837
00:41:23,440 --> 00:41:24,920
It's not for myself,

838
00:41:25,280 --> 00:41:26,440
but for you

839
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:27,400
and Ai Chen.

840
00:41:28,760 --> 00:41:29,800
Seeing Ai Chen

841
00:41:30,280 --> 00:41:32,280
worry so much about your treatment,

842
00:41:33,590 --> 00:41:34,960
I wanted to do something

843
00:41:34,960 --> 00:41:35,840
to help her.

844
00:41:37,000 --> 00:41:39,130
I just wanted to set an example for you.

845
00:41:40,230 --> 00:41:41,840
If I can be cured,

846
00:41:42,320 --> 00:41:44,450
then you definitely can be cured, too.

847
00:41:48,280 --> 00:41:49,280
If you get better,

848
00:41:50,630 --> 00:41:51,830
Ai Chen will be happy,

849
00:41:53,510 --> 00:41:55,070
and I can rest easy, too.

850
00:42:07,630 --> 00:42:09,890
But the moment I stepped into this house,

851
00:42:10,070 --> 00:42:11,630
I thought of your mom.

852
00:42:13,670 --> 00:42:15,630
Seeing you looking so sickly

853
00:42:16,880 --> 00:42:18,540
reminded me of your mom saying

854
00:42:18,880 --> 00:42:20,280
how much she loved you,

855
00:42:21,230 --> 00:42:23,290
worried about you, and cared for you.

856
00:42:26,110 --> 00:42:27,710
I couldn't bear to force you.

857
00:42:29,510 --> 00:42:30,670
So I changed my mind.

858
00:42:40,550 --> 00:42:41,360
Zhengliang.

859
00:42:43,510 --> 00:42:44,970
Let's stop the treatment.

860
00:42:46,550 --> 00:42:47,880
Some scars

861
00:42:48,230 --> 00:42:49,590
just can't heal.

862
00:42:50,670 --> 00:42:51,670
If you can move on,

863
00:42:52,230 --> 00:42:53,710
there's a way to live.

864
00:42:54,440 --> 00:42:55,590
If you can't,

865
00:42:55,800 --> 00:42:57,800
there's a way to live with that, too.

866
00:42:59,320 --> 00:43:00,590
Nothing matters more

867
00:43:01,710 --> 00:43:03,190
than life itself.
